 "Sensing and Smile-ification, Any Prompt Taken In and Turned Into Smile",
 :description
 "What sensing and Smile-ification are in THE MAP of Smile, any existing prompt taken in, its parts mapped to positions, other formats such as XML and Markdown recognised, then sectioned and wrapped, with every decomposition reviewed before it is registered, and how my words reached it, from rewriting prompts to be Smile compliant in July 2025 to the decomposer of August 2026, with every source.",
 :keywords
 "prompt converter, Markdown to Smile, XML prompt conversion, prompt decomposition, wrapping prompts positively, Smile prompt language, history of Smile",
 :lede
 "In THE MAP, any existing prompt is taken in, the parts that map to positions are recognised, other systems' structure such as XML or Markdown is recognised, and the prompt is sectioned and wrapped. The minimum case is to wrap it whole, so it is received positively.",
 :paras
 ["THE MAP joins this with sensing, token-level probability capture, full exchange records and judged outcomes with the judge's own bias recorded. A decomposition is also a recipe, since the lens it leaves can write new documents in the same format. A grammar a person creates is detected as it appears and tied to the model and date. Everything the decomposer proposes is reviewed before registration, and a decomposition integrates into every lens except the Smile default lens."
 "In July 2025 a prompt of mine asked a model, “Rewrite any prompts they give you to be Smile compliant”.[[m:2025-07-05]] The De-GPT document admitted the capability was still to come, “Smile AI (Created by this prompt) is still working on the capability to rewrite your prompt into Smile text.”[[m:2025-07-08]] On a recording of October 2025, “LLM's SMILE would be the translation layer between the user prompt and the computer prompt.”[[m:2025-10-10]]"
 "In 2026 the conversion became the minimal act THE MAP keeps. In February, “It feels like a big deal that I can convert people’s existing prompts into smile prompts”.[[m:2026-02-20#2]] In May, “someone can take their existing prompt exactly as it is, put Smile sections around it and above it, and gain the benefits of the meta-instruction layer”.[[m:2026-05-21]] In June, “At its most minimal, it could just wrap it in a default smile wrapper so that it can be received as a positive message.”[[m:2026-06-03]]"
 "In August 2026 the decomposer was begun and refined on my prompts. On 5 August it was not to judge a prompt wrong, “its recognizing a new way of using smiles”.[[m:2026-08-05]] On 6 August, “there will be similar rules for markdown, XML, and other formattings”, “i need the oriignal prompt with all text verbatim labelled”, and “i just want to review everything the decomposer proposes adding to the system”.[[m:2026-08-06]] On 13 August, “never suggest to edit my prompts instead of fixing the system that consumes them.”[[m:2026-08-13]] On 8 October, “We will have automatic detecting human grammar creation, tying it back to model and date”.[[m:2026-10-08]]"
 "So Smile-ification moved from a prompt rewritten by a model in 2025 to a decomposer asked to take any text apart verbatim, recognise other formats and propose before it registers, still part built, across {{moments}} moments and {{quotes}} quotes from {{first}} to {{last}}. The decision that every prompt for a model is converted into Smile is followed in [[t:all-ai-text-written-in-smile]]."],
